what = IntroWhat(
  "A component workshop that turns each component state into a runnable, isolated example (a story) written in Component Story Format (CSF), then layers on interactive Controls, auto-generated Docs, accessibility checks, and automated visual and interaction testing.",
  "Storybook is an open-source tool for building UI components and pages in isolation. It runs as a separate workshop environment alongside your app, rendering each component state — called a story — from a plain code file so you can develop, document, and test without wiring up screens, mock servers, or app state.",
  [
    "Stories, not screenshots: every state is live, executable code in Component Story Format (CSF)",
    "Isolated development: render a single button without booting routes, auth, or backend data",
    "Interactive controls: tweak args and argTypes to explore component states instantly",
    "Built-in safety net: play functions, test runner, and visual regression catch regressions in CI",
  ],
  ["Storybook", "UI Components", "Design System", "Component Testing", "Frontend Tooling"],
)

why = IntroWhy(
  "Developing components inside a running app means booting the whole system — login flows, API mocks, feature flags — just to see one button in its error state. Untested, undocumented components then drift silently between PRs and break production pages.",
  "Storybook shrinks the feedback loop to a single component state, makes every state reviewable as documentation, and converts stories into automated tests — so design-system regressions are caught on the pull request instead of by users in production.",
)
